cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pydfine in your research, please cite both this software and the original D-FINE paper."
title: "pydfine: a config-first, ultralytics-style Python library for the D-FINE detector"
abstract: >-
  pydfine is a batteries-included, config-first Python port of the D-FINE real-time object
  detector. The entire model is configured through typed Python parameters on one class,
  with numeric parity against the upstream released checkpoints.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "pydfine contributors"
url: "https://github.com/HoshiBatista/pydfine"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HoshiBatista/pydfine"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-07-18"
keywords:
  - object-detection
  - d-fine
  - detr
  - computer-vision
  - pytorch
  - onnx
